|> Exercise
    work=ing
    handle=_cosine_rule_geometric_2_

    Keeping the diagram of Exercise >>_cosine_rule_geometric_1_,
    find a formula for $c$ in terms of $a$, $b$  
    and $\theta_{ab}$.

    |> Solution

        By Exercise >>_cosine_rule_geometric_1_,
        these rectangles have the same area:

        |> Image
            src=images/_e5_cosine_rule_geometric_2_sol1.svg

        !! By symmetry, 
        But by a similar argument,
        these rectangles 
        !! also 
        can also be shown to have
        have the same area:

        |> Image
            src=images/_e5_cosine_rule_geometric_2_sol2_v2.svg

        This gives...

        |> Image
            src=images/_e5_cosine_rule_geometric_2_sol3.svg

        ...thiiiis...

        |> Boxed
            $$
            c = \sqrt{a^2 + b^2 - 2ab\cos\theta_{ab}}
            $$

        ...formula!
